      "event": {
        "id": 53728270164669,
        "title": "3rd Annual Purdue + Google AI Summit",
        "url": "https://www.purdue.edu/events/ai-summit/",
        "updated_at": "2026-10-12T20:54:29-04:00",
        "location": "Westin Indianapolis",
        "room_number": "",
        "location_name": "Westin Indianapolis",
        "status": "live",
        "experience": "inperson",
        "kind": "standalone",
        "address": "241 W. Washington St., Indianapolis, IN 46204",
        "recurring": false,
        "free": false,
        "private": false,
        "ticket_cost": "$425 before Sept. 25; $25 for students",
        "description_text": "AI Impact: From Possible to Proven\n\nPurdue University and Google are sponsoring the 3rd Annual Purdue + Google AI Summit, organized by Purdue\u2019s Institute for Physical AI. This year\u2019s summit will focus on the shift from AI experimentation to execution, exploring how industry leaders, government agencies, and Purdue researchers are driving tangible outcomes and scaling real-world AI applications.\n\nJoin us for keynotes, breakout sessions, hands-on Google AI tool demos, exhibits, and networking designed for both technical and non-technical leaders. Program themes will include industry execution, next-generation technical and research frontiers, the future of work, and the evolving role of AI in education and the public sector.\n\nKeynotes featuring national leaders in AI, industry, and public policyIndustry-focused discussions on manufacturing, defense, agriculture, pharmaceuticals, drug discovery, transportation, and spaceTechnical sessions covering AI systems, semiconductors, cybersecurity, physical AI, quantum technologies, and research frontiersHands-on workshops and demonstrations, including Google AI toolsExhibits showcasing innovations from leading companies, Purdue research centers, startups, and student organizationsNetworking opportunities designed for both technical and business audiencesWhether you're leading AI adoption, developing next-generation technologies, conducting cutting-edge research, or preparing the workforce for the future, the AI Impact Summit offers an opportunity to learn from peers, discover new ideas, and build valuable connections.\n\n\nThis year\u2019s speaker lineup will be announced soon. Past keynotes included Purdue President Mung Chiang, Google Public Sector CEO Karen Dahut, Waymo VP Srikanth Thirumalai, and US Senator Todd Young. Previous presentations included leading experts from Bayer, Eli Lilly, Caterpillar, Cummins, Corteva, L3Harris, Saab, Boeing, IU Health, and more.\n\nRegister by September 25 for $175 off the standard registration fee of $600\n\n(Student registration: $25)",
        "geo": {
          "latitude": "39.76634",
          "longitude": "-86.163816",
          "street": "241 West Washington Street",
